      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-163059",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the function $f(x,y)$ and the region $D$ given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={x}^{2}+2y+1,\\,D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 3}.\n$$\n\nAccording to the mean value theorem for double integrals, there exists a point $(a,b)\\in D$ such that the volume of the solid enclosed between the surface $z=f(x,y)$ and the $xy$-plane over the region $D$ equals the volume of the right cylinder with base $D$ and height $f(a,b).$ Find $b$ given that $a=1.$"
